From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] HACK: mm: Allwinner sun5i AHB/MBUS bus-stall workaround in memmap_init_range

On Allwinner sun5i SoCs (R8/A13, NextThing C.H.I.P.), initialising the
page map via memmap_init_range() writes 131072 struct page entries in a
sustained burst to DRAM.  After the burst, the AHB/MBUS bus arbiter
retains unresolved write transactions; the very next DRAM read (e.g.,
loading a printk format string from .rodata) stalls the CPU indefinitely.

The same failure class was fixed in U-Boot:
  env/nowhere.c   - DSB + 50 ms before himport_r()
  lib/hashtable.c - 5 ms udelay per himport_r() iteration
  boot/image-fdt.c - DSB + 5 ms between each FDT fixup step

Apply the equivalent workaround for the kernel:

1. Inside the memmap_init_range() loop: mb() + short busy-wait every
   256 pages (pfn & 0xff == 0) so the AHB arbiter can drain between
   bursts of struct page writes.

2. After the loop: mb() + 2 M-iteration busy-wait to allow the bus to
   return to idle before the first post-init printk.

Temporary diagnostic pr_notice included to confirm the function
completes — remove once boot is stable.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
 mm/mm_init.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/mm_init.c b/mm/mm_init.c
--- a/mm/mm_init.c
+++ b/mm/mm_init.c
@@ -903,6 +903,11 @@ void __meminit memmap_init_range(unsigned long size, int nid, unsigned long zone
 #endif

 	for (pfn = start_pfn; pfn < end_pfn; ) {
+		/* sun5i AHB/MBUS settle: periodic barrier during heavy DRAM writes */
+		if ((pfn & 0xff) == 0) {
+			mb();
+			{ volatile int __d; for (__d = 0; __d < 100000; __d++); }
+		}
 		/*
 		 * There can be holes in boot-time mem_map[]s handed to this
 		 * function.  They do not exist on hotplugged memory.
@@ -939,6 +944,10 @@ void __meminit memmap_init_range(unsigned long size, int nid, unsigned long zone
 		}
 		pfn++;
 	}
+	/* sun5i AHB/MBUS settle: DSB + busy-wait after heavy DRAM writes */
+	mb();
+	{ volatile int __d; for (__d = 0; __d < 2000000; __d++); }
+	pr_notice("[MM-DBG] memmap_init_range done pfn %lu\n", pfn);
 }

 static void __init memmap_init_zone_range(struct zone *zone,
